body:
Held work for #1947: this session cannot write under `.claude/`. A write there needs an approval prompt, and the session is not interactive. The PR does all other parts of the issue. A session with write access to `.claude/skills/` must apply this patch to `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.

1. In "Status of Gaps from #356", add two rows after the "Live GUI session" row:

```markdown
- **Document units (#578):** Shipped via `set_units`.
- **Program number and comment (#258):** Shipped via `set_program`.
```

2. Replace all of the "Known Remaining Gaps" section body (the three numbered items and the *Note*) with:

```markdown
No GUI command is known to lack its MCP tool. Per `AGENTS.md`, a command PR that does not bundle an MCP tool files a `source:agent` issue titled `MCP: <command>`, labelled `P5` and `area:mcp`. List such an open issue here until its tool ships. Name only the command and the issue in this section, never a tool.
```

The three old items are shipped:

- `SetupAlign`: `lay_part_on_face`.
- `SetUnits`: `set_units`.
- The program header (#258): `set_program`.

3. Under "## Tool Reference", add this line after the first paragraph:

```markdown
The complete generated list, with every argument, is `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (`camcraft-cli mcp reference`). A local model takes `camcraft-cli mcp prompt`.
```

4. Add this pin to `crates/app/tests/mcp_doc_drift.rs`. It fails on the current skill: `post, set_part_axes, lay_part_on_points, lay_part_on_face, set_wcs_from_features, set_units`.

```rust
#[test]
fn the_known_gaps_name_no_shipped_tool() {
    let skill = read(".claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md");
    let start = skill.find("## Known Remaining Gaps").expect("the skill keeps its gaps section");
    let rest = &skill[start..];
    let gaps = &rest[..rest.find("\n---").unwrap_or(rest.len())];
    // Each word, and each CamelCase command (`SetUnits`) read as snake_case.
    let mut words: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
    for w in gaps.split(|c: char| !(c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || c == '_')) {
        words.push(w.to_owned());
        let mut snake = String::new();
        for (i, c) in w.chars().enumerate() {
            if c.is_ascii_uppercase() && i > 0 {
                snake.push('_');
            }
            snake.push(c.to_ascii_lowercase());
        }
        words.push(snake);
    }
    let shipped: Vec<_> =
        catalog::tool_names().into_iter().filter(|n| words.iter().any(|w| w == n)).collect();
    assert!(shipped.is_empty(), "the Known Remaining Gaps list names shipped tools: {}", shipped.join(", "));
}
```

This is a process-file change. Its PR needs the line `Process change: yes`.
